      "problem": "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}-{j}^{2})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}-{j}^{2}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}-{j}^{2})] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(({i}^{2}-{1}^{2})+({i}^{2}-{2}^{2})) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(({i}^{2}-1)+({i}^{2}-4)) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(2{i}^{2}-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(2{i}^{2}-5) & =(2(1)^{2}-5)+(2(2)^{2}-5)+(2(3)^{2}-5) \\\\  & =-3+3+13 \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$",
